# Firebase web config — copy to .env.local and fill in from
# Firebase console → Project settings → Your apps → Web app.
# Vite embeds these at BUILD time; the app cannot reach Firebase without them.
#
# These are optional: the same six values are committed as source in
# src/firebaseConfig.js, and src/firebase.js falls back to them for anything
# blank or absent here. A non-blank value here wins, which is how you point a
# local build (or a Vercel deploy) at a different Firebase project.
#
# Write env files in UTF-8. PowerShell's `Set-Content -Encoding utf8` adds a
# byte-order mark, Vite's parser does not strip it, and the FIRST line then
# silently disappears — that is how a deploy once lost its API key.
#
# Project id for this repo: beacon-edu-consult-proj (see .firebaserc).
# The project id is not a secret — it ships in the client bundle — but the
# values below are per-app, so copy them from the console rather than guessing.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
